cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HistoRange, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "HistoRange: Histology-Defined Continuum Transport for Spatial Cell-Cell Communication and Signaling Range Inference"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Su
    given-names: Jiayu Ellie
    affiliation: Phillips Academy, Andover, Massachusetts, USA
repository-code: "https://github.com/JiayuEllieSu/HistoRange"
url: "https://github.com/JiayuEllieSu/HistoRange"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  HistoRange is a computational framework for spatial transcriptomics that uses
  registered H&E histology to define a spatially varying anisotropic transport
  geometry for secreted ligand signaling. It separates spatial association
  detection from post-detection effective-range estimation, so that a fitted
  scale is reported quantitatively only when the data support it.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - cell-cell communication
  - ligand-receptor signaling
  - H&E histology
  - finite element method
  - signaling range
